# Tor onion-service config template. The entrypoint substitutes __PORT__ with the port Apache
# actually listens on (Render injects $PORT) and writes the result to /etc/tor/torrc, then starts
# tor only when ENABLE_ONION=1. We are NOT a Tor client here — SocksPort 0 disables that.
SocksPort 0
Log notice stderr
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
User debian-tor

# v3 onion service pointing at the local Apache. The address is derived from the key in
# HiddenServiceDir; the entrypoint installs a provided key there (from a Render Secret File) so the
# address stays STABLE across restarts. Without a provided key, tor generates a throwaway one.
HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/hidden_service
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:__PORT__